This is the ESTATE's log for this vendor fork, and it is not upstream's
CHANGELOG.md. Upstream owns that file and every merge overwrites it; this one
records only what the estate did and why, so the fork's own history survives
the next 79-commit merge.

## the Amber Bus mark is back, and this time it tells the truth

The mark that says this AdGuard is the estate's fork had quietly stopped
existing. Upstream PR 2715 moved CLIENT_DIR from client/ to client_v2/, and
the mark lived in client/ — preserved byte-for-byte by the merge, compiled by
nothing.

Rebuilding it surfaced the more interesting problem: the old one was static
markup with title="Amber Bus connected", rendered unconditionally. It claimed
the connector was connected whether or not a token was configured, so it
would have read "connected" throughout precisely the outage it existed to
report. A decorative indicator is worse than no indicator, because people
believe it.

The replacement reads real state. GET /control/status now carries a
fork-local `amber_bus` block — invoke path, exposure mode, and whether the
connector token is actually set — and the mark renders from it: nothing at
all on a server that does not publish the block, and "Amber Bus not
configured" when the token is missing. That last state is the one worth
showing: an unset token falls through to session auth, so bus calls are
rejected and nothing else in the UI would say so.

Two things worth knowing for the next person in here. client_v2 is SolidJS,
not React, so anything carried over from client/ is a rebuild and not a port.
And the mark had to go in the Sidebar as well as the Header, because the
Header is display:none above 1200px — putting it only where the old one lived
would have made it invisible on every desktop.

Also adds amber_bus.client.version.json. The bus manifest has always declared
local_manifest_required and named that exact file, and it did not exist, so
nothing was reporting the fork's connector version at all. framework_version
stays 0.4.0: that is current, per amber-bus CLIENT_FRAMEWORK_VERSION, and the
0.4.6 in the bus's native_client_manifest is a different artifact with a
version line of its own — the two are not comparable.

Verified by asking whether the artifact actually contained the change, rather
than whether the build was green: the new label appears in the built binary,
which it did NOT before the build ordering was fixed in the Hub's registry
the same day. | Operator Agent
